 "check_text": "protocol.py: 1 biology problem (1 warning).\n\n1. WARNING COLD-MODULE-NEVER-SET: A temperature module was loaded but never set\n   line 37:  p300_single.dispense(50, block[well])\n   At line 37 the robot puts liquid into wells A1, A2, A3, A4, A5, A6, A7, A8 and 40 more in\n   slot 2, on a temperature module that the protocol never sets. A temperature module stays\n   at room temperature until `set_temperature` is called, so protein (sample) sat on a block\n   that was never cold; the robot pipetted there 48 times over the run. The person setting\n   up the deck sees a module and assumes it is cold. Wells: wells A1, A2, A3, A4, A5, A6,\n   A7, A8 and 40 more in slot 2.\n   Affected: wells A1, A2, A3, A4, A5, A6, A7, A8 and 40 more in slot 2.\n   Fix: Call `temp_module.set_temperature(4)` before the first transfer from Opentrons 96\n   Well Aluminum Block with Generic PCR Strip 200 \u00b5L in slot 2, and\n   `temp_module.deactivate()` at the end.\n   Source: Opentrons, temperature module: at room temperature until set_temperature, which\n   blocks\n           https://docs.opentrons.com/v2/modules/temperature_module.html\n   Source: Thermo Fisher T4 ligase manual: keep on ice, use within minutes\n           https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/LSG/manuals/t4dnaligase_1U_man.pdf\n   Source: NEB: Q5 High-Fidelity PCR kit manual (add the polymerase last)\n           https://www.neb.com/-/media/nebus/files/manuals/manuale0555.pdf\n   [aecf3b356b10]\n\nThe Opentrons simulator (8.8.2) passed this protocol with no error: it checks that the robot\ncan make the moves, not what they do to the liquids.",
